/*
    To semi-formalize the English Statement into a structure of premises and conclusions, we will examine the English Statement sentence by sentence, and break down each sentence into natural language clauses that are as atomic as possible.
*/

{
    "premises": [
        /*
        The sentence "There is a quadrilateral □TUWV with a diagonal line TV." first declares a quadrilateral □ T U W V with TV being a diagonal.

        From the instructions, we know that all points and lines are distinct, so it declares 4 distinct points: T, U, W, V that form a quadrilateral □ T U W V with TV being a diagonal.

        It also declares a line TV that is a diagonal of the quadrilateral □ T U W V.

        Therefore, we can convert the sentence into the following 2 premises:
        */
        "The distinct points T, U, W, V form a quadrilateral □ T U W V with TV being a diagonal",
        "T and V are distinct points on line TV",
        /*
        By definition of a quadrilateral, any 3 of its 4 vertices must not be collinear, so we also expressed the fact that the lines TU, WV, TW, UV, TV are all distinct.

        Therefore, we checked that all distinctness relations among points and lines are expressed.
        */

        /*
        The sentence "∠ U T V ≅ ∠ T V W and ∠ V T W ≅ ∠ T V U." states congruence relations between 2 pairs of angles: the angles ∠ U T V and ∠ T V W are congruent, and the angles ∠ V T W and ∠ T V U are congruent.

        Therefore, we have the following 2 premises:
        */
        "The angles ∠ U T V and ∠ T V W are congruent, denoted as ∠ U T V ≅ ∠ T V W",
        "The angles ∠ V T W and ∠ T V U are congruent, denoted as ∠ V T W ≅ ∠ T V U",
    ],
    "conclusions": [
        /*
        The sentence "Complete the proof that T W ≅ U V." states the goal of the proof: to show that the line segments TW and UV are congruent.

        Therefore, we have the following conclusion:
        */
        "The line segments TW and UV are congruent, denoted as T W ≅ U V"
    ]
}
